# READ REPLICAS ARE TSERVERS. They run YSQL backends, so they need kmoney on their own
# filesystem -- the catalog reaches them through `CREATE EXTENSION`, the shared library does not.
# Every other YB suite here uses primary nodes only, so this whole class of node had no evidence
# behind it, and a read replica is exactly the node someone forgets: it is not where writes go.
[doc("kmoney on a read-replica placement: it needs the library too, and fails loudly without it.")]
test-yb-readreplica tag="" replicas="1":
